~ start
if ProgressMarkers.has_met.Francesca == false
	Lucius: Mrs. Esteban, how are you feeling?
	Francesca: You’d like to ask me some questions, I suppose. Please Just give me a moment. 
	Lucius: Of course. Take your time.
	Francesca: …
	Francesca: Alright. What would you like to know, detective?
	do ProgressMarkers.has_met.Francesca = true
else
	Francesca: Detective? Is everything alright?
	Lucius: I’d just like to ask you a few more things.
=> questions
~ questions
Francesca: -
- What did you do this morning?
	Francesca: Let’s see. I prepared his lunch, made sure he was dressed properly, prepared Anna for school, dropped her off with that anthrocat, then went home.
	=> questions

- How did you prepare his food today? [if ProgressMarkers.has_asked.Homecooking /]
	Francesca: Ah well. I must confess that I’m not really a good cook. I wanted to prepare something for him, but I just couldn’t figure it out.
	do unlock_keyword("Delivery", "noun")
	Francesca: I kind of panicked and just ordered chicken from Min’s Restaurant and called it my own.
	=> questions

- Do you know anyone with a personal vendetta against your husband?
	Francesca: He’s unfortunately made a few enemies with the public because of his work. You can’t really blame him. It’s hard trying to please everyone.
	Lucius: What about the people close to him?
	do unlock_keyword("Gary", "name")
	do unlock_keyword("Ortolano", "name")
	Francesca: Hmm. He did often bring up that Secretary Ortolano. They had different opinions about how to handle their work.
	do unlock_keyword("call", "verb")
	do ProgressMarkers.has_asked.Night_Call = true
	Francesca: He actually called last night. I don’t know what they talked about, but at one point, Benjamin started laughing and said something like, "You really are thickheaded. You brought this on yourself. Don’t bring me into it."
	Francesca: He then hung up. He seemed pretty happy after that.
	Lucius: So Secretary Ortolano. Anyone else come to mind?
	Francesca: Other than that. I don’t particularly like his secretary. She speaks all polite, but I know she dislikes us. I can see it in her eyes.
	do unlock_keyword("Drive", "verb")
	do unlock_keyword("Home", "noun")
	Francesca: And to think I let her drive me and my daughter to her school. She really is bad luck.
	=> questions

- Can you tell us anything about these documents? [if ProgressMarkers.has_found.Vault_Documents /]
	Francesca: How did you-
	Francesca: Listen. I did not partake in the COCHE scandal in any way, do you understand?
	Lucius: Of course. Of course.
	Lucius: However, many of these documents discuss controversial events. If someone were to hate your husband, we may be able to find a clue about who it is in here.
	Francesca: But-
	Lucius: If we can narrow it down to a few documents, then we don’t need the rest. We can just leave them here. Otherwise, we might have to bring all of them.
	Francesca: …
	Francesca: Well, as long as it stays between you and me. He made sure that a lot of those events never made it to the news. The only one that he failed to completely hide was his work in the extrajudicial killings.
	do unlock_keyword("Extrajudicial Killings", "noun")
	Francesca: If one of the events caused his death, it’s most likely that one.
	=> questions

- So, how’s Drew these days? [if ProgressMarkers.has_asked.Drew_Relationship and ProgressMarkers.has_asked.Drew_Date /]
	Francesca: Wha- why are you bringing him up all of a sudden?
	Lucius: Just my curiosity. As a detective, I just like knowing things.
	Francesca: He’s doing well. He’s landed a big role in a new movie, and he plans on running for the Senate in the next election.
	Lucius: You sure know a lot about him.
	Francesca: Well, we stayed friends after our divorce. After all, we split up because we both wanted different things. Not because we hated each other.
	Lucius: Is that why you met with Mr. Sangster today? Just to keep in touch?
	Francesca: What do you mean? Meeting with Drew? I was at home the entire day.
	Lucius: I see, then that person with Mr. Sangster must have just been someone very similar to you. My mistake.
	do unlock_keyword("Met", "verb")
	Francesca: It’s alright. Though, I am curious why you thought it was me meeting with Mr. Sangster.
	Lucius: Actually, it wasn’t me who saw them. I was interrogating a suspect earlier, and she said she saw someone who looked like you with Mr. Sangster during lunch.
	Francesca: Well, I can assure you that it wasn’t me. I don’t even like coffee.
	Lucius: [i](I see.)[/i]
	Lucius: [i](I never mentioned that he was seen at a cafe.)[/i]
	Lucius: Of course. Witness reports can sometimes be unreliable, especially where faces are involved.
	=> questions

- Thank you for your time.
	=> END